  -> T* PREDICTS A KNOWN FAILURE MODE: rho=+0.575 (p=0.0277, n=15) against repetition under greedy decoding, a measurement sharing no machinery with the ring construction. T* becomes a cheap scalar with external meaning, obtainable in four settle runs. SEPARATELY, and this part IS clean: models that never concentrate average rep_4=0.572 against 0.509 for those that do -- indistinguishable. So the attractor BINARY has no predictive value for repetition at all; whatever signal exists is in T* as a graded quantity within the concentrating group, not in whether a model concentrates.

